Below the form, the same **External link** section lists the links that are still alive. A revoked link, or one whose date has passed, leaves the list entirely — so "not there" means "not working".

Each row carries:

- the mode it was made with — **Anyone with the link**, **Password-protected**, or **Email-gated** with the number of addresses;
- its expiry in words: *Expires in 12 days*, *Expires today*, *No expiry*;
- a view count, *0 views* until someone opens it;
- icon buttons whose tooltips read **Copy link** — on rows whose URL Bee Flow can still recover — plus **Re-snapshot — update the public copy to match current edits** and **Revoke link**.

Colleagues who can read the page see this list read-only: no recipient addresses, no creating, no revoking.

One row can be special. If the page has a public address, that address is served by one of these links — revoke that row and the address stops serving too. Revoking any other row leaves it untouched.
